</section>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.3 </span>Pruning on Quantized Models</h3>

<div id="S3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For VLMs, we can begin pruning image tokens at two stages: one at the vision encoder and the other at the language model component. We input the image and text pairs to collect each output token’s attention score distribution <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> in different layers. For the vision encoder, we use <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\mathrm{img}}^{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>img</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\mathrm{img}}^{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> to donate the attention score of the <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th token in the <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>-th layer. For the language model part, we follow FastV <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite> to use <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\mathrm{sys}}^{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>sys</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\mathrm{sys}}^{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\mathrm{txt}}^{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>txt</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\mathrm{txt}}^{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\mathrm{out}}^{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\mathrm{out}}^{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> for system prompt, image tokens, user instruction, and output tokens. For the vision encoder we have:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\mathrm{img}}^{i,j}=1," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>img</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\mathrm{img}}^{i,j}=1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For the language model we have:</p>
<table id="S3.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\mathrm{sys}}^{i,j}+\alpha_{\mathrm{img}}^{i,j}+\alpha_{\mathrm{ins}}^{i,j}+\alpha_{\mathrm{out}}^{i,j}=1" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>sys</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>img</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>ins</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\mathrm{sys}}^{i,j}+\alpha_{\mathrm{img}}^{i,j}+\alpha_{\mathrm{ins}}^{i,j}+\alpha_{\mathrm{out}}^{i,j}=1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Then we calculate the token attention score to obtain the salient tokens, take image token for example, the attention score of image tokens in layer <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> is:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\mathrm{img}}^{j}=\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{n}\alpha_{\mathrm{img}}^{i,j}}{N_{\mathrm{img}}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>img</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>img</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>img</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\mathrm{img}}^{j}=\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{n}\alpha_{\mathrm{img}}^{i,j}}{N_{\mathrm{img}}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathrm{img}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>img</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathrm{img}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of image tokens, <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of tokens in the response.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Results and Comparisons</h2>

<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
